\text{The coefficient of } x \text{ is } -4, \text{ so:} & a(2) = -4 \implies a = -2. \\
\text{Therefore the quadratic polynomial is:} & -2(x^2 + 4x + 13) = -2x^2 - 8x - 26.
\end{align*}
\begin{answer}
-2x^2 - 8x - 26
